<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01957</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>2dc75ddd-e9f1-4ffe-b7a9-f619b4660a45</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>Explain how the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> in <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> affect the graph of the equation.</item>
  <item>Explain how graphs, tables, and equations that represent the same quadratic function are related.</item>
</list>
<para id="para-00002">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>7.12.1: Using Coefficients and Constant Terms to Identify Graphs of Linear Equations
    <list id="list-00003">
      <item>In this activity, you matched three linear equations with their graphs by comparing slopes and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts.</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>7.12.2: Transformations with Quadratic Functions
    <list id="list-00004">
      <item>In this activity, you explored how transformations affect the graphs of quadratic functions.</item>
      <item>7.12.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>7.12.2: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>7.12.3: Understanding the Behaviors of a Graph in Relation to Its Quadratic Expression
    <list id="list-00005">
      <item>In this activity, you examined the values in tables and how the values from a quadratic expression affect its graph.</item>
      <item>7.12.3: Self Check</item>
      <item>7.12.3: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>7.12.4: Representations of Quadratic Functions
    <list id="list-00006">
      <item>In this activity, you used the standard form and factored form of quadratic functions as well as their graphs to identify intercepts to match the equivalent forms and their graphs.</item>
      <item>7.12.4: Self Check</item>
      <item>7.12.4: Additional Resources</item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations
    <list id="list-00007">
      <item>In this activity, you matched the graphs of quadratic functions with their equations.</item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list id="list-00008">
  <item>7.12.6: Practice</item>
</list>
<section class="checking-in" id="sect-00002"><title>Checking In</title><exercise id="e6226166-f14b-4a92-83ca-75f5f8b4bed8" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00004">On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para></problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00005">Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
